# f03: the options path, over BOTH options screens.
# menu-top: three DOWNs to OPTIONS, A -> menu-options.
#
# AUDIO (MENU-SPEC §4; new this arc — the row used to emit `refused
# audio`): A on AUDIO -> options-audio. RIGHT x2 raises Sounds 0.5 -> 0.7,
# DOWN moves to Music, LEFT drops it 0.3 -> 0.2; shot; B saves both levels
# (audiomenu.js:24-25, no meHost gate) and returns with the cursor still on
# AUDIO. There is no A handler on that screen at all (audiomenu.js:16-121),
# so none is scripted.
#
# GAMEPLAY (MENU-SPEC §3.1; the row list is upstream's complete five):
# DOWN to GAMEPLAY, A -> options-gameplay. Row 0 turbo ON; DOWN, A, A =
# L-cancel 0->1->2; DOWN, A = Flash on L-Cancel ON; DOWN, A = Everyone
# Walljumps ON (the measured-dead toggle — row + bit, wired to nothing);
# DOWN to Tapjump off (row 4, the only multi-column row), A = P1, RIGHT +
# A = P2. B backs to menu-options (cursor GAMEPLAY), B to menu-top (cursor
# OPTIONS), DOWN wraps 3->0 (VS. MELEE — the wrap witness), then the
# default-chars launch: VS. MELEE -> css (C5) -> START -> sss -> A
# (battlefield, marth vs marth, edited settings).
# Bridge mode `state`: BRIDGE-STATE proves the edited settings reached the
# GameState slice. The LAUNCH line gained `flashlcancel=1 walljump=1`
# (MENU-SPEC §13.1 item 1, and review-r2 asked for it): every OTHER field
# is byte-unchanged from the pre-arc freeze — turbo=1 lcancel=2
# tapjump=1,1,0,0 — so the manifest cross-binds still bind the same values,
# and the two new columns are the evidence that the two new rows reach the
# bridge at all.
